From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:29:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] selftests: apple-dcp: take the Aurora harness and follow the
 j604 tree

The DCP host selftests no longer built on the integrated tree: 36 of
57 units failed, all at compile time (MEASURED, run.py on ecb6c069d9).
f55cd56508 synced drivers/gpu/drm/apple to Aurora 50d5865ea6 file by
file but left the fixtures behind, and later J604 integration work moved the
sources further. The apple-afkv2 runner did not build either, and the
standalone m4-error-paths.py and plane-layout.py programs failed.

Take apple-dcp and apple-afkv2 from Aurora 50d5865ea6. That harness
already covers 31da169251, b0effd1c9b, b7c75a932a, dbb6bcce98 and
the 9ec757d1fb half of 75c2dd5b6c. On top of it, keep the selftest
parts this tree adds:
- 1f20dc769c, 2bb760e6c4: m4 HDR check and panel VRR stubs
- 167ddf5b79: oslog echo flag
- 0f9cf89e4e: route sleep_parked
- 11c43d2f98: ATC mux and restore helpers
- bfe8de8b77: DPMS power-off stub
- 579bc680ee: dwc3 deep-sleep state, teardown shutting_down
d77c55666a's fixture change is not needed. Aurora's harness models the
panel dimensions itself.

Then follow what this tree has and Aurora lacks:
- m4: dcp-m4-frame.h includes the EDR swap words and maps the 10-bit
  fourccs, so the m4 units take dcp-edr.h and dcp-m4-edr.h with host
  shims. m4-dpms-retirement models the EDR, raised-SDR-white, flip
  cadence, power-gate and BT.2020 state of iomfb_m4_swap(), _present()
  and _blank(), all off, and uses the real iomfb_m4_boost_ceiling().
- display: the flip-paced brightness ramp needs max() and clamp().
- dcp-panel-adt.c: one host form for the three units that compile it.
  The phram ADT reader, an OF and memremap leaf, is dropped.
- oslog-events: model oslog_owed and cover the echo contract. An owed
  counter is echoed once and cleared; any other counter is not echoed.
- rate fixtures: the dead M4 get_modes branch now calls
  iomfb_m4_panel_edid() and dev_warn_once().
- dwc3: model the T8140 hibernation setup as an MMIO leaf.
- m4-error-paths: the DART units take the real
  apple_dart_fail_borrowed() macro. The PMP readiness unit answers for
  J604 beside J713 and for the T8122 legacy wait.
- plane-layout: the plane state carries pixel_blend_mode.
- Stubs for code only one of the two trees has are marked unused, so one harness builds on both trees.
- j616s-panel-identity reports a TAP SKIP when the tree has no
  t6040-j616s.dts. run.py never counts a skip as a pass.

No assertion is relaxed.

Result on this tree (MEASURED):
- run.py: 86 ok, 1 SKIP, 0 not ok of 87. All 57 units of the previous
  harness are ok (before: 21 ok, 36 not ok).
- m4-error-paths.py: 8 of 8 ok. plane-layout.py: control build valid,
  every case passes. Both failed before, on Aurora's tree as well.
- apple-afkv2: run-afkv2-tests.sh 116 ok, 0 not ok (before: no
  build); test-admission.py passes.
Same harness on Aurora 50d5865ea6: run.py 87 of 87 ok,
m4-error-paths.py 8 of 8, plane-layout.py valid.

